&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Summit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit Therapeutics Inc. is a biopharmaceutical oncology company with a mission focused on improving quality of life, increasing potential duration of life, and resolving serious unmet medical needs. At Summit, we believe in building a team of world class professionals who are passionate about this mission, and it is our people who drive this mission to reality. Summit’s core values include integrity, passion for excellence, purposeful urgency, collaboration, and our commitment to people. Our employees are truly the heart and soul of our culture, and they are invaluable in shaping our journey toward excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit’s team is inspired to touch and help change lives through Summit’s clinical studies in the field of oncology. Summit has multiple global Phase 3 clinical studies, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi: Phase 3 clinical study which was intended to evaluate ivonescimab combined with chemotherapy compared to placebo plus chemotherapy in patients with EGFR-mutated, locally advanced or metastatic non-squamous NSCLC who were previously treated with a 3rd generation EGFR TKI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-3: Phase 3 clinical study which is intended to evaluate ivonescimab combined with chemotherapy compared to pembrolizumab combined with chemotherapy in patients with first-line metastatic NSCLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-7: Phase 3 clinical study which is intended to evaluate ivonescimab monotherapy compared to pembrolizumab monotherapy in patients with first-line metastatic NSCLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Colorectal Cancer (CRC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-GI3: Phase 3 clinical study intended to evaluate ivonescimab in combination with chemotherapy compared with bevacizumab plus chemotherapy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ivonescimab is an investigational therapy not presently approved by any regulatory authority other than China’s National Medical Products Administration (NMPA). Summit is headquartered in Miami, Florida, and has additional offices in California, New Jersey, the UK, and Ireland.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt;&quot;&gt;Job Title: Sr. Medical Science Liaison&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt;&quot;&gt;Location: Oxford, UK or Zug, Switzerland or Dublin, Ireland&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Clinical Supply Management supports the Senior Director in leading the full scope of global clinical supply chain responsibilities. The role translates functional strategy into disciplined execution across demand and supply planning, inventory management, packaging and labelling, distribution, returns and destruction, cross-border compliance, and GxP operations. Acting as a key delegate for the Senior Director, the (Associate) Director provides a layer of management for direct reports, establishes clear priorities and performance expectations, develops team capability, and drives operational excellence through standardized processes, meaningful metrics, proactive risk management, and continuous improvement. The role partners closely with Clinical Operations, Commercial, CMC, Quality, Regulatory, Finance, Legal, Procurement, Medical Affairs and Program Management, and oversees external partners including Contract Development and Manufacturing Organizations (CDMOs), IXRS providers and specialist service providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the Senior Director in developing functional strategy, operating plans, budgets, governance and performance objectives across global clinical supply chain activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads day-to-day execution for new and ongoing studies and products, ensuring robust forecasting, supply planning, schedule adherence, inventory optimization, global logistics and sustained GxP compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as a delegate for the Senior Director in cross-functional forums, governance meetings, supplier reviews and issue escalation, providing clear recommendations and ensuring timely follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages and develops direct reports, translating functional priorities into individual objectives, balancing workloads, coaching performance, supporting career development and ensuring appropriate succession and capability plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates an effective management layer by coordinating team activities, reinforcing accountability, removing operational barriers and escalating material risks or decisions to the Senior Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing the Clinical Supply Management (CSM) team, the Associate Director interprets complex clinical protocols, development plans and commercial demand forecasts, working with CMC and internal and external partners to develop packaging, labelling, supply and resupply strategies, timelines and plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the accountability of CSM team to oversee packaging, labelling, release, distribution, resupply, returns, reconciliation and destruction activities across global locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops and maintains supply project budgets, resource plans and integrated schedules, monitors performance and proactively resolves variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages CDMO and service-provider activities from RFP and contracting support through routine operations, troubleshooting, invoicing and performance management using defined KPIs and service expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports IXRS selection, design, set-up, User Acceptance Testing (UAT), implementation and ongoing operational performance as required by IRT Management Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives operational excellence by defining standard work, governance routines, KPIs and dashboards; uses trend and root-cause analysis to improve service, quality, cost, compliance and team productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads continuous-improvement initiatives that streamline and harmonize processes, strengthen inspection readiness and embed sustainable ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports regulatory submissions, audits and inspections and ensures timely management of SOPs, change controls, deviations, investigations and CAPAs within the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides continuity of leadership and performs other responsibilities within the function as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience, Education and Specialized Knowledge and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc, MSc, engineering or pharmacy degree, or equivalent, with a minimum of 8+ years of progressive supply chain experience in a pharmaceutical, biotechnology or contract development and manufacturing organization (CDMO) environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex international clinical studies and product supply chains, with broad knowledge of regulatory and GMP requirements for IMP and commercial product packaging and supply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior people-management experience, including setting objectives, coaching performance, developing talent, delegating effectively and managing through others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate strategy into executable priorities, operating rhythms, metrics and measurable team outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational-excellence and continuous-improvement capability, including process standardization, KPI management, root-cause analysis and sustainable implementation of improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of IXRS design specifications, set-up and UAT, together with proficiency in clinical supply planning and forecasting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project, budget, risk and resource-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining high-quality results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in outsourcing, supplier governance, negotiation and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, scaling or improving end-to-end product supply chains and associated business processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate as a trusted deputy to the Director, exercise sound judgement within delegated authority and escalate issues with clear options and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator able to influence all levels of the organization and build effective relationships with global colleagues, customers and suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work independently with complex global problems while fostering inclusion, collaboration, accountability and effective team leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile and resilient in a dynamic organization where priorities may change rapidly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the drug development process and applicable FDA, EMA and PMDA expectations, including GMP, GCP, Annex 13 and relevant clinical trial requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically proficient with industry-standard systems and tools and able to use technology, data and industry trends to improve efficiency and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable of and compliant with SOPs, change controls, deviations, investigations and CAPAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the pay for this position&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$83,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$97,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, depth of experience, certifications, and specific work location. This may be different in other locations due to differences in the cost of labor. The total compensation package for this position may also include bonus, stock, benefits and/or other applicable variable compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit does not accept referrals from employment businesses and/or employment agencies in respect of the vacancies posted on this site. All employment businesses/agencies are required to contact Summit’s Talent Acquisition team at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- obtain prior written authorization before referring any candidates to Summit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Summit Therapeutics Inc.&amp;nbsp;is an Equal Opportunity Employer and takes pride in creating and maintaining diverse environment. We do not discriminate in recruitment, hiring, training or promotion or any other employment practices for reasons of race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, disability, or any other legally protected status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Our Purpose&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SentinelOne, we are driven by a clear purpose: to give the advantage to those who secure our future. As AI reshapes how organizations build, operate, and innovate, the responsibility to protect them becomes more critical than ever. When you join SentinelOne, your work helps protect global enterprises, critical infrastructure, and the technologies shaping tomorrow. If you are motivated by meaningful challenges and want your impact to be real, measurable, and global, you will find purpose here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SentinelOne is a company at the intersection of AI and security, pioneering a new operating model for cybersecurity. Our AI-native platform unifies protection across endpoint, cloud, identity, data, and AI systems to deliver autonomous detection and response with clarity and speed. By combining real-time analytics, intelligent automation, and a unified data foundation, we reduce noise, simplify complexity, and empower security teams to focus on what truly matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams are builders, problem-solvers, and innovators committed to shaping the future of security. If you are excited to solve hard problems alongside talented, mission-driven people, we invite you to help us build a safer future for humanity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Are We Looking For?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people who are relentlessly curious and committed to continuous learning. AI is reshaping every function across our business, and we enable every team member, regardless of role or level, to build fluency in AI tools and concepts. Those who thrive here actively seek out new solutions, experiment thoughtfully, and apply what they learn to drive better, faster, smarter outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;As a Sr. Solutions Engineer, you will be tasked with driving adoption, building strong partner relationships, and evangelizing our solutions across the region. You will focus on enabling the MSSP ecosystem, positioning and integrating SentinelOne&#39;s technology within partner technical offerings, selling to the managed partner base, conducting demos, delivering technical training, Proof of Values, assisting partners with pre and post sales activities, and assisting with escalations. Your role will be responsible for managing our MSSP partners, while cultivating long-term relationships with partners, and the SentinelOne field and Product/Engineering teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What will you do?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Primary responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Managed partner team to identify and qualify partnership opportunities, identify key partner technical objections, competition, and develop strategies to resolve technical blockers and scale the partner sales business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring feedback from partners and end customers to product management to improve the SentinelOne&#39;s solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive follow-ups with partner resources to consistently deliver on messaging how SentinelOne adds value to the partner and their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and create go-to-market initiatives and offerings with SentinelOne partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute technical training plans for partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical relationship with SentinelOne&#39;s partners, and the coordination of additional technical resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver demonstrations and work hands-on with partners to demonstrate SentinelOne&#39;s value in the partner&#39;s environment or solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What skills and knowledge should you bring?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;10 Years+ in field, 5+ years Sales Engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Exceptional track record of growing managed partner technical resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong background in building relationships with internal sales and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience presenting and delivering technical demos and sales values presentations to varying audiences from architects to C-level executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Technical experience/skills for the successful candidate:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience working with CSPs, channel, MSP/MSSPs, GSIs, or alliances partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ability to quickly learn, adapt, understand, and work with new emerging technologies, methodologies and solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Fluent Dutch and English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Willingness to travel up to 50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why SentinelOne?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is redefining how the world operates and rewriting the rules of security in real time, and SentinelOne was built for this moment. From day one, we architected an AI-native platform designed to operate at machine speed, not as an add-on to legacy systems but as the foundation itself. If you want to build where innovation and impact move together, this is that place.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our Sentinels with comprehensive, competitive benefits designed to support you and your family:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity &amp;amp; Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restricted Stock Units (RSUs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan (ESPP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off &amp;amp; Wellbeing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive leave benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gender-neutral parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance &amp;amp; Financial Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insurance and medical allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program (EAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Perks &amp;amp; Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global home office allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mobile phone reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuter or work-from-home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness &amp;amp; Lifestyle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;SentinelOne is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;SentinelOne participates in the E-Verify Program for all U.S. based roles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team’s mission is to align Vinted’s values, business goals, and Employer Value Proposition with our people’s real work experience. We translate Vinted’s truth into an inspiring story that attracts the right people, helps them grow, and instils them with pride.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take an active role in Employer Branding at Vinted, with a particular focus on attracting engineering and data science talent. You’ll be based in Amsterdam, where our data science team is growing, but your work will reach candidates around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vinted has become an ecosystem with vertically integrated shipping and payments. This requires us to adapt our EVP to three very distinct brands and even more diversified hiring needs. Your job is to turn that into creative campaigns and stories that make specific audiences want to work here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our next big focus is storytelling. Bringing the skills and challenges our teams face to life! What is a day in the life of a cybersecurity analyst? How does an anti-money laundering expert keep members’ wallets safe? What does it take to build the data science behind a marketplace used by millions? And what stories does each of our locations need?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partnering with Talent Acquisition, engineering and data science leaders, People, Marketing, PR, Internal Comms, and Brand &amp;amp; Design, you’ll make sure those stories are told and that our presence is strong where we hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the guardian of Vinted’s employer brand, ensuring consistency and visibility across all platforms, like LinkedIn and Instagram&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong brand-building skills, with a clear vision of global vs local branding differentiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use your sound understanding of branding and our editorial guidelines to write clear and engaging copy for things such as blogs, advertising campaigns, employer branding assets, email campaigns, event materials, online company profiles, as well as our careers pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create bespoke or support partnership events such as meetups, webinars, and networking events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and run recruitment advertising, such as targeted LinkedIn campaigns and sponsorships with third-party publications and organisations, aimed at technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define where our global employer brand ends and local adaptation begins, so each location can tell its story while staying consistent with Vinted’s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape our content calendar around hiring needs and our location strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track what works, using results to sharpen the next activation, and share learnings with the wider Employer Branding team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about all things Employer Branding!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love storytelling: finding stories and having a keen eye for telling them in ways that stand out. You can show campaigns or activations you conceived and delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
